{{Synced switch
|version1 = [[File:Chugging barrel (disassembled) detail.png|150px|left]]
|version2 = [[File:Chugging barrel detail.png|150px|left]]
}}
The '''chugging barrel''' is a tradeable item that allows players to consume up to five potions in a single click. It is purchased from the [[Mixology Rewards]] shop at a cost of  17,250 [[Mox resin]], 14,000 [[Aga resin]], and 18,600 [[Lye resin]]. It is sold in a disassembled state (where it cannot store potions); players must use the 'Assemble' option in order for the barrel to become useable. The player is not required to have done the [[Mastering Mixology]] mini-game to assemble it. The barrel is only tradeable in its disassembled state.  While the assembled barrel is untradeable, it is possible to dismantle the barrel at any time, although doing so will cause all potions currently stored inside to be lost.

The barrel can be filled by using up to five different potions on the item itself or via the bank loadout interface; a maximum of 100 doses per potion can be stored. Players can set up to four different loadouts in a bank for the barrel, as well as reorder the potions consumed, filling, and emptying the barrel. Potions and [[Potions#Barbarian_Mixes|barbarian mixes]] can be stored, but [[Hunter's mix|hunter mixes]] cannot. Reordering potions allows players to consume potions in a specific order, such as [[Saradomin brew]]s before [[super restore]]s, allowing for stats to be boosted correctly. Vials will not be consumed after using all the contents inside the vial. When loading from presets, the barrel will pull from whichever interface is opened (i.e, if looking at potion storage when loading, the barrel will pull potions from pot storage). While it may be beneficial for certain players to place their [[super attack]], [[Super strength|strength]], and [[Super defence|defence]] potions inside the barrel and drink it as if it were a [[super combat potion]], it is recommended to buy super combat potions since they are cheaper than the barrel.

'''The barrel may only be used within a [[bank]] or next to a [[bank chest]].''' Certain bank interfaces do not allow the use of the barrel.{{Fact|Some were fixed on 12 August 2026, are there any banks where it still doesn't work?}} 

[[Ultimate Ironmen]] are able to store potion doses inside the chugging barrel and consume potions from it. However, they cannot set loadouts as it requires the use of a bank interface to do so. Its contents are also preserved even when the barrel is lost or deleted on death, able to be accessed after assembling a new chugging barrel. This allows it to be used for [[ghost storage]], although due to the time investment to reobtain the barrel, this is not very useful.

The chugging barrel cannot be stored in [[Chambers of Xeric]] storage if accidentally brought into the raid. A disassembled chugging barrel can be stored in a [[Looting Bag]].

